s `db:create db:migrate`. Docs, three ADRs (two inferred), four skills, AGENTS.md, a CI workflow running uw-harness verify, a pre-push hook, compose.yaml, .env.example and .tool-versions were added. Seven open questions (deploy, observability, contribution process, CI, default database, skipped tests) are TODO blocks.\n\n**Assessment.** Redmine is a flexible, open-source project management web application built with Ruby on Rails. Stack: Ruby (>= 3.3, < 4.1; CI tests 3.3, 3.4, 4.0), JavaScript (Stimulus controllers via importmap), CSS, Perl (extra/svn/Redmine.pm), Rails 8.1.4, Hotwire Stimulus (stimulus-rails) with importmap-rails, Propshaft asset pipeline, Doorkeeper (OAuth2 provider), Minitest with mocha, Capybara + Selenium (system tests), RuboCop (+performance, +rails), Stylelint, Puma (server in tests and install docs). The full assessment stays in `.git/uw-harness/assessment.md` on the machine that ran uw-harness.\n\nRisks seen before the harness:\n\n- The Gemfile reads config/database.yml (git-ignored) to choose database gems: without that file, bundle install warns and no database adapter is installed, so setup and every gate fail.\n5:## Notes from the harness build\n15:## 2026-11-01: harness built by uw-harness 0.3.0 with claude","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013LQGJtLj2TPZu1s6Hn8VNP","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgcvzkshhshvvk4LCmAKQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QAdkoa4tk4u6APTLdk6FPb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> docs/harness/log.md <<'EOF'\n\n## 2026-11-01: wiki toolbar syntax moved to the browser (#43259)\n\nWhat changed: the server no longer renders the syntax of the wiki toolbar buttons. `Redmine::WikiToolbar` subclasses only give `format_name` (`common_mark` or `textile`) and `groups` of button names; the base class renders spacers between groups, `data-wiki-toolbar-format-value` on the root, `wiki-toolbar#apply` with `data-wiki-toolbar-button-param` for normal buttons, `toggleMenu` for `table` and `precode`, `insertPrecode` with `data-wiki-toolbar-lang-param` for each language, and one generic `keydown->wiki-toolbar#shortcut` action. Shortcut keys (b, i, u) are in `Redmine::WikiToolbar::SHORTCUTS`. The syntax of each format (buttons, table cells, code block) is the exported `formats` object in `app/javascript/controllers/wiki_toolbar_controller.js`.\n\nWhat I learned: Stimulus key filters such as `keydown.ctrl+b` require the exact set of modifiers, so the generic `shortcut` action checks itself that only Ctrl (Cmd on macOS) is pressed, to keep the old behavior (Ctrl+Shift+B does nothing). `bin/rails` uses the macOS system Ruby 2.6 unless PATH contains the Homebrew Ruby; `bin/harness` fixes PATH only for its own tasks. The `frontend-stimulus` skill mentions `app/javascript/wiki_formatting/`, which does not exist.\n\nWhat is left: a plugin text formatter that uses the toolbar must now add its syntax to `formats` in JavaScript; there is no documented extension point for that yet. The system tests (`test/system/wiki_toolbar_test.rb`, `test/system/keyboard_shortcuts_test.rb`) pass locally with headless Chrome, but `bin/harness check` does not run them.\nEOF\ngit status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1978,"cache_read_input_tokens":81831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1978},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc4df5e4-a75f-4eef-8855-4e8a00111d19","uuid":"7592ffec-a66e-4186-b621-f730317cf4d8","timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:38:53.310Z","request_id":"req_011CgcvzkNhEBHnEo96A4sbw","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QAdkoa4tk4u6APTLdk6FPb":{"command":"cat >> docs/harness/log.md <<'EOF'\n\n## 2026-11-01: wiki toolbar syntax moved to the browser (#43259)\n\nWhat changed: the server no longer renders the syntax of the wiki toolbar buttons. `Redmine::WikiToolbar` subclasses only give `format_name` (`common_mark` or `textile`) and `groups` of button names; the base class renders spacers between groups, `data-wiki-toolbar-format-value` on the root, `wiki-toolbar#apply` with `data-wiki-toolbar-button-param` for normal buttons, `toggleMenu` for `table` and `precode`, `insertPrecode` with `data-wiki-toolbar-lang-param` for each language, and one generic `keydown->wiki-toolbar#shortcut` action. Shortcut keys (b, i, u) are in `Redmine::WikiToolbar::SHORTCUTS`. The syntax of each format (buttons, table cells, code block) is the exported `formats` object in `app/javascript/controllers/wiki_toolbar_controller.js`.\n\nWhat I learned: Stimulus key filters such as `keydown.ctrl+b` require the exact set of modifiers, so the generic `shortcut` action checks itself that only Ctrl (Cmd on macOS) is pressed, to keep the old behavior (Ctrl+Shift+B does nothing). `bin/rails` uses the macOS system Ruby 2.6 unless PATH contains the Homebrew Ruby; `bin/harness` fixes PATH only for its own tasks. The `frontend-stimulus` skill mentions `app/javascript/wiki_formatting/`, which does not exist.\n\nWhat is left: a plugin text formatter that uses the toolbar must now add its syntax to `formats` in JavaScript; there is no documented extension point for that yet. The system tests (`test/system/wiki_toolbar_test.rb`, `test/system/keyboard_shortcuts_test.rb`) pass locally with headless Chrome, but `bin/harness check` does not run them.\nEOF\ngit status --short"}}}
