{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgcw1LCB7GCXfnEjnY2Lu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DrbjAkYBV3ZdLYsC13i5XA","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"status":"done","summary":"The toolbar syntax now lives in JavaScript. The server markup only says which buttons exist and how they are grouped. In Ruby, each text formatter's WikiToolbar subclass now has two methods: `format_name` ('common_mark' or 'textile') and `groups` (lists of button names). The base class Redmine::WikiToolbar renders the new contract: a `data-wiki-toolbar-format-value` attribute on the root, a spacer between groups, `wiki-toolbar#apply` with `data-wiki-toolbar-button-param` for normal buttons, `toggleMenu` and its menu parameter for `table` and `precode`, `wiki-toolbar#insertPrecode` with `data-wiki-toolbar-lang-param` for each precode language, and `wiki-toolbar#help` for the help button. The root has exactly three keyboard actions: `keydown->wiki-toolbar#shortcut` and the two Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+P preview toggles. Only strong, em and ins carry `data-wiki-toolbar-shortcut` (b, i, u). In wiki_toolbar_controller.js, an exported `formats` object defines, for common_mark and textile, the inline and line syntax of each button, the table header and separator cells, and the code block syntax by language. The values are the same as the old Ruby values. New actions `apply` and `insertPrecode` replace `wrap` and `wrapLines`, and `insertTable` reads the active format. Stimulus key filters like `keydown.ctrl+b` only match the exact set of modifiers. So the generic `shortcut` handler checks this itself: only Ctrl is pressed (Cmd on macOS). This keeps the old behavior, for example Ctrl+Shift+B still does nothing. The full gate `bin/harness check` passes, and the toolbar and keyboard-shortcut system tests pass in headless Chrome. Nothing was committed.","changes":[{"path":"lib/redmine/wiki_toolbar.rb","summary":"Renders the markup contract from format_name and groups: format value, spacers between groups, apply/toggleMenu/help actions, button/menu/lang params, SHORTCUTS for b/i/u, and fixed KEYBOARD_ACTIONS (generic shortcut plus two preview toggles). Removed the code that turned button options into Stimulus parameters."},{"path":"lib/redmine/wiki_formatting/common_mark/helper.rb","summary":"WikiToolbar now only defines format_name 'common_mark' and its groups of button names."},{"path":"lib/redmine/wiki_formatting/textile/helper.rb","summary":"WikiToolbar now only defines format_name 'textile' and its groups of button names."},{"path":"app/javascript/controllers/wiki_toolbar_controller.js","summary":"Adds the exported `formats` (syntax of each button, table and code block for common_mark and textile), a `format` value, the actions apply and insertPrecode, insertTable based on the format, and a generic shortcut handler that checks the modifiers. Removes wrap, wrapLines and menuParams."},{"path":"test/unit/lib/redmine/wiki_toolbar_test.rb","summary":"Tests the new contract for both formatters: format value, button order and spacers, actions and params, no syntax params in the HTML, exactly three keyboard actions, shortcuts only on strong/em/ins, and the precode lang param."},{"path":"test/integration/layout_test.rb","summary":"The precode menu check now looks for data-wiki-toolbar-lang-param instead of the prefix param."},{"path":"test/system/wiki_toolbar_test.rb","summary":"New browser tests: every syntax button for both formatters (including heading replacement), and the Textile highlighted code menu."},{"path":"test/system/keyboard_shortcuts_test.rb","summary":"New browser test: modifier+Shift+B and modifier+D do not insert anything."},{"path":"docs/harness/log.md","summary":"Dated entry: what changed, what I learned, what is left."}],"acceptance":[{"criterion":"The toolbar renders with the new contract for CommonMark and Textile","met":true,"evidence":"test/unit/lib/redmine/wiki_toolbar_test